<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Damian Hugo Philipp von Schönborn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1676">1676</a>–<a href="/years/1743">1743</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Damian Hugo von Schönborn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Damian Hugo Philipp von Schönborn was a German churchman of the powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schonborn-family">Schönborn family</a>, made a cardinal in 1715. As prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Speyer from 1719, he moved the bishops' residence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippsburg">Philippsburg</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruchsal">Bruchsal</a> and built the baroque palace there. He reformed the administration and finances of his small state, and from 1740 he was also prince-bishop of Constance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damian-hugo-philipp-von-schonborn.jpg" alt="Damian Hugo Philipp von Schönborn" width="320" height="500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugo,_Kardinal_von_Sch%C3%B6nborn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The bishops ruled a territory on both banks of the Rhine but not the city of Speyer, which became a free imperial city; they moved their residence to Udenheim, renamed Philippsburg, and in 1720 to Bruchsal, where Cardinal <b>Damian Hugo von Schönborn</b> built a baroque palace.</blockquote><a href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-speyer">Prince-Bishopric of Speyer</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruchsal">Bruchsal</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=50,8.27&amp;year=1719" aria-label="Mainz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4740 424 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Damian Hugo Philipp von Schönborn"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5190 694h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5190 694h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=50,8.27&amp;year=1719">What was here in 1719? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
